  "deviceAcceptance": false,
  "note": "Chrome CPU-throttle proxy for an iPhone XS Max (414x896 @3, mobile profile); GPU work is not throttled. Other sessions kept the host 22-66% busy, so the step-2 and step-3 builds were alternated in two rounds under the same conditions instead of comparing with docs/testing/hmh-perf-crowd-baseline.json. Round 1 ran the --sourcemap builds of both commits (byte-identical to the round-2 --sourcemap builds), round 2 ran plain builds for timing and --sourcemap builds for profile passes. rAF intervals are vsync-quantised, so the simulation cost per fixed tick from the CPU profiles and the pinned headless digest timing are the direct measures.",
  "change": {
    "guards": "c31b5990: positive, nonNegative, nonNegativeInteger, positiveInteger, validSeed, point2/point3 and the lexical id comparator were copied into up to twelve simulation modules; they now live once in value-guards.mjs with identical bodies and messages. value-guards gains cellKey, a collision-free packed integer key for grid cells within +-8191 (string \"x,y\" beyond).",
    "groundQueries": "elevation.mjs: samples are built frozen (shared flat up-normal) instead of deep-walked by freezeDeep; createAuthoredGroundQuery looks up a 256-unit cell list of the surfaces whose padded box touches the cell, in priority order, and falls back to the full scan unless every surface is frozen geometry. Swept traversal results freeze field by field.",
    "separation": "enemy-simulation.mjs: packed integer cell keys, one neighbourhood list per occupied cell, scratch arrays instead of one object per candidate, and a k-smallest cut instead of sorting every candidate; the rank, the rounding neighbourhood at the cut, the exact Math.hypot distances and the (distance, id) order are the release rule. stepEnemyPopulation reads deltas by index (id-keyed fallback for repeated ids), skips the id re-sort of the formation map, memoizes stableHash, and freezes intents/results shallowly where every nested value is already frozen.",
    "blockerIndex": "blocker-bounds.mjs: bucket merge with a per-index stamp and packed keys instead of Set + string keys + sort; querySourceOrder returns candidates in the caller's array order.",
    "projectiles": "projectile-physics.mjs: cover is narrow-phased only when the immutable blocker index and a padded box test say the segment can reach it (visited in the caller's order); resolveProjectileBatch validates ids, builds the id map and sorts targets once per batch instead of once per shot; the hurtbox grid uses packed keys and no per-bucket sort; frozen hurtbox profile shapes are validated once.",
    "melee": "melee.mjs: createMeleeTarget freezes shallowly (both grounds are frozen points)."
  },
